// FIXED — aug18a class 4 (katana divergence_000000): kernel per-slot
// state survived a SHRINK-TO-ZERO resize. Every in-loop chain ensure
// (DynCall cache pairs, per-slot call-site blocks, select-table
// directory levels below an outer loop) was emitted per-iteration
// INSIDE the loop body, so a zero-length epoch never ran the
// truncate and the regrow saw no length change — per-slot count
// state continued where the interp's slot.delete built fresh.
// THE SHRINK-TO-ZERO RULE (Ruling 2's slots-are-activations applied):
// each loop's ALWAYS-EXECUTED exit block re-ensures every chain
// claimed within its body at its own level (`TruncRec` records,
// close_slot_tables stash → emit_slot_truncates, propagating outward
// frame by frame), truncating exactly when the interp deletes the
// slot activations. No prewalk: the exit block is as always-executed
// as the preheader the parked plan wanted, and close time has every
// record naturally.
// Face 2 — nested levels: an OUTER len-0 epoch skips the inner
// preheader entirely; the outer exit now truncates the directory and
// frees the inner subtrees. Pre-fix interp [4,0,4] / jit [4,0,8].
{let x = array::iter([i64:2, i64:0, i64:2]); array::fold(array::init(x, |i| array::fold(array::init(i64:2, |j| j), i64:0, |a: i64, e: i64| a + count(e))), i64:0, |acc: i64, v: i64| acc + v)}
